WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.240
- All right, y'all so we've
reached the end of the hour,

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.120
but don't worry, I have one last story.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.970
I hope you enjoy.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:05.959
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.959 --> 00:00:09.300
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.133
All week.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:11.440
We're celebrating Rad Mamas

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.680
but Rad Mama doesn't mean perfect mom

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.770
coz that doesn't exist

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.230
and if you think you are one,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.740
you're definitely not.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.810
Coz no one's a perfect parent,

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.110
but motherhood is tough,

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.350
and these last two years
have been especially hard.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.610
More and more moms struggle with anxiety,

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.160
and that can be difficult
to explain to kids,

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.130
and their big feelings to put into words.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.240
So that's why I really
appreciate a new children's book.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.480
Children's book rather
written by two mamas.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.800
It's called "Sometimes Mommy is Anxious.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.910
A little book about Big feelings."

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.990
We have the mamas who wrote it dialed in.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.560
So everybody say hi to Marci

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.907
and Lindsay who watch
on NBC 10, Philadelphia.

00:00:46.907 --> 00:00:50.138
(crowd cheering)
(clapping)

00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:51.270
Hi ladies.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.750
So Marci, I'm gonna start with you.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.310
So this is such a great idea for a book.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.910
So how did you come up with it?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.230
- So I'm a mom of two and so is Lindsay.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.700
And I really started
having trouble with anxiety

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.080
and mental health issues
after I had children

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.980
and Lindsay suffered her
whole life pretty much

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:07.290
since she was a teenager

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.040
and she's always been my go to

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.610
our husbands have been best
friends since they were five.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.390
So we really leaned on each other.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:15.050
And I went over her house one day

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.670
and our two little boys

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.260
who are only four months apart,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.093
were playing a game

00:01:19.093 --> 00:01:20.750
where they kept bringing us books to read.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.420
And she was like, wouldn't
it be great if there was

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.000
a book out there for that
mental health that we

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.070
can describe, you know, to
the kids what's going on

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.850
and why mommy's feeling this way.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.890
And we looked and we
couldn't find anything

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.010
and so we decided to write one(laughing).

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:34.843
- Here we are.

00:01:34.843 --> 00:01:35.676
(laughing)
- I love that.

00:01:35.676 --> 00:01:38.600
So Lindsay, what do you hope
children get out of the book

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.260
- So really we just wanted to help fight

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.530
the stigma that surrounds mental health.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.140
So many children really just don't know

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.070
that it's okay when you're
not feeling your best.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.650
We had our book and we wanted to describe

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:57.080
and show different races and body types

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.120
and cultures and just show

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.720
that anxiety doesn't discriminate

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.410
and that a lot of mother

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.510
and children could see
themselves in this book,

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:09.160
and we have had such a
great response thus far.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.753
So many mothers and our friends.

00:02:10.753 --> 00:02:12.760
- It's exciting
- It's so exciting.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.640
- Yeah.
- It's a really cool idea.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.356
So thank y'all for doing this.

00:02:16.356 --> 00:02:17.223
(crowd clapping)

00:02:17.223 --> 00:02:18.320
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.100
- We just want our kids to know it's okay.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.340
Not to be okay.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.173
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:22.173 --> 00:02:23.760
It's so it's such a great message.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.400
So everybody pick up a copy

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.070
of "Sometimes Mommy is Anxious" on Amazon.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.230
Thank you so much, Marci.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.110
Thank you so much, Lindsay.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.203
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:31.203 --> 00:02:32.036
(crowd clapping)

00:02:32.036 --> 00:02:33.076
- [Lindsay] Oh, thank you Kelly.

00:02:33.076 --> 00:02:34.803
- [Marci] Thank you
- Thank you for having Us.

00:02:34.803 --> 00:02:35.817
- Absolutely.

